# Support Ticket Desk - Notes

## 1. Which state lives in Redux, which in Context, which in local component state, and why.

Redux is used for manage tickets and shared the data between components

context is used at them to be shared between components instead of passing it vaia props

## 2. How your optimistic update and rollback work, step by step.

If the status changed for example from open to closed . the new value appeared at the ui before getting successful response from the API . if the api failed apply rollback in the ui


## 3. Why your filter selectors are memoized, and what would happen without createSelector.
It used to filter tickets and calculate status counts.
It remembers the previous result and avoids unnecessary calculations
when the input data has not changed.

Without memoization, filtering could create a new array on every
selector execution, potentially causing unnecessary component
re-renders.

## 4. One thing to be improved if i have time ?
If I have more time, I would improve the UI, add more features, and remove duplicated data by using the mock API and shared types consistently across the application.